110
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Û em dibînin ku maşallah zêde, dar û bar in, xweza xweşik
e...
 
And we see that Mashallah, there are many trees, the nature
is beautiful...

111
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Ne hemdulillah, rebûl alemin, temam e wekî hûn dibînin.
 
No, praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, it's perfect as
you can see.

112
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Em gelekî kêfxweş bûn. Ji te razî be, em xatirê te dixwazin.
Ez zehf kêfxweş bûm, bi dîtina te. Dest û çavên te maç
dikim.
 
We are very happy. May God be pleased with you, we bid you
farewell. I was very happy to see you. I kiss your hands and
eyes.

113
00:08:44,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Xwedê ji te razî be, xwedê we... spas, te rûmet da, ser
seran û ser çavan... Wele.
 
May God be pleased with you, God... thank you, you gave
honor, upon heads and upon eyes... By God.

114
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Em mezin bûn li vî gundî
 
We grew up in this village

115
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Her tiştê xweş me tê da dît
 
We saw everything beautiful in it

116
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Çiqas sal j'omrê me çûn
 
No matter how many years of our lives passed

117
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Me nizanî çawa derbas bûn
 
We didn't know how they passed

118
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Tên ber çavan rûyên şêrîn
 
Sweet faces come before my eyes

119
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Digrîn j'wan wextên şêrîn
 
Crying for those sweet times

120
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Çi xweş bû zemanê paşî
 
How beautiful were the times of the past

121
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Çîrokên tijî bextewarî
 
Stories full of happiness

122
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
Tên bîra min
 
They come to my mind

123
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
Şefeqa sibê radibûn
 
They used to wake up at dawn

124
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Dengê dîkan re şa dibûn
 
They would rejoice at the rooster's crow

125
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,000
Azana sibê radibûn
 
They used to wake up to the morning call to prayer

126
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Her kes bi kar û şixulê xwe dibûn
 
Everyone was tending to their work

127
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Qîz û xort hev kom dibûn
 
Girls and boys would gather together

128
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Bi ken û kêfxweş rê ve diçûn
 
With laughter and joy, they would set off

129
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Şivanan kar û bar dikirin
 
Shepherds were doing their chores

130
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Heval bûn, xwişk û bira bûn
 
They were friends, sisters, and brothers

131
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Tên bîra min
 
They come to my mind

132
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Tamşevanên me yê ezîz, destpêkê vîdyoyê me ji we ra xeber da
bû ye, ka em derbasî baxçê hinaran bibin.
 
Our dear viewers, at the beginning of the video we told you
that we would visit the pomegranate orchards.

133
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Ev baxçe jî em ketin nav gundê Kaniyê Gewrkê.
 
The orchard we entered is in the village of Kaniye Gewrke.

134
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Di gundê Kaniyê Gewrkê da du baxçê hinaran tenê heye, ev
baxçê hinara yê ku em ketin nav jî yê malbeta Evdî Qumo ye.
 
There are only two pomegranate orchards in the village of
Kaniye Gewrke, and the one we entered belongs to the family
of Evdi Qumo.

135
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Niha jî em ê biçin cem dayê rûniştin, dayê jî maşallah dest
pê kar dike.
 
Now we will go sit next to the mother, she is starting to
work, mashallah.

136
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Xwedê emrêkî dirêj bide te, dayê. Sibeha we bi xêr, dayê.
 
May God give you a long life, mother. Good morning, mother.

137
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Hela û sehlan anê, tu çawa yî rûhê min?
 
Welcome dear, how are you, my soul?

138
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Baş î, tu çawa yî?
 
Are you well? How are you?

139
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Hemdullah. Tu çawa yî, qenc î? Rind î, rehet î?
 
Thank God. How are you, are you well? Are you fine, are you
comfortable?

140
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Wela emel e, hemdullah.
 
Well, it is an action, thank God.

141
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Navê te nas bikin.
 
Let us know your name.

142
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Navê min Fehîme ye.
 
My name is Fehime.

143
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Hemşka Hesen Garkî me.
 
I am the wife of Hesen Garki.

144
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Dayîka Hesen, tu çawa yî?
 
Mother of Hesen, how are you?

145
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Hemdullah.
 
Thank God.

146
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Dema we çawa ye îsal?
 
How is your season this year?

147
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Wela ev e em tê da dikin.
 
Well, this is it, we are working in it.

148
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Hemdullah.
 
Thank God.

149
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Em rehet in di nav hinaran da re. Û îsal erzan in jî.
 
We are comfortable among the pomegranates. And they are
cheap this year.

150
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Hinar in, me pir zerar kir wela.
 
They are pomegranates, we suffered a lot of loss, by God.

151
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

152
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Û dîsa hemdullah, ji bela vê ji Xwedê bî ne ya qul bî.
 
And still, thank God, as long as the trouble is from God and
not from His servant.

153
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Dayîka Hesen, me bala xwe dayê hinên we li zeytûna jî
qewişîne erdê, hin hinar in, û pel û wa tişt in.
 
Mother of Hesen, we noticed you have swept some olives to
the ground, some are pomegranates, and leaves and such
things.

154
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Tûlya lê kir, wez li gund da hiltan. Ev a tûlya wek lê
kiribû.
 
Tûlya hit it, we were picking it in the village. It was like
Tûlya hit it.

155
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Dîsa hemdullah, ji Xwedê ye, Xwedê quwetkê bide we, û sihhet
û afiyetê bide.
 
Still, thank God, it's from God, may God give you strength,
and grant you health and well-being.

156
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Xwedê quwetê bide te jî anê.
 
May God give you strength too, dear.

157
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Tu li kî derê dikişînî? Kamera tê. E wa... Erê wa, wî...
 
Where are you shooting? The camera is coming. Hey there...
Yes there, him...

158
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Dayê ew keşkên we ji me re xeber dan çend roj in hûn dest bi
hinara kirine?
 
Mother, those girls told us, how many days have you been
starting on the pomegranates?

159
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Buxudê, ev e îro du roj in em berhev dikin.
 
By God, it's been two days today that we are gathering.

160
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Ev yê ber malê jî sê roj a me berhev kir.
 
We gathered the ones in front of the house for three days as
well.

161
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Îro em di vira da ne, em xelas bikin.
 
Today we are here to finish it.

162
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Du rojê me li ber malê jî hene wî alî da.
 
We also have two days in front of the house on that side.

163
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Kîlo bi çendê ye?
 
How much is a kilo?

164
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Buxudê, ton bi sêsed û pêncî dolarî da, ne bi kîlo ye.
 
By God, a ton is given for three hundred and fifty dollars,
not by kilo.

165
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Em bala xwe didinê dayê ew paqijiyê hin hûn başqe dikin,
dimis başqe...
 
We are noticing, mother, that you separate the clean ones,
the syrup ones separately...

166
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,000
Ê paqij bi şeş warqa didin, difiroşin.
 
They give the clean ones for six bills, they sell them.

167
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Hûn difiroşin gî...
 
You sell them all...

168
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Em nafiroşin gî. Qesab tê dikişîne...
 
We don't sell them all. Someone brings it for us and weighs
it...

169
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Û evna jî giyê zêrokê ne...
 
And these are the ones for the yellow syrup...

170
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Evna yê... em li giyan ji lev kin.
 
These... we will separate them from the weeds.

171
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Xwedê stûran bide bilê tu rûniştî be.
 
May God protect you, sit down.

172
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Evana, evên di nav qulekê di wî de... ewey qers...
 
These, the ones you saw in the molds... the big ones...

173
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Xwedê ji te re bihêle, emrêkî dirêj bide we.
 
May God keep them for you, and give you a long life.

174
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Te xeber da, ji taybetî we ra...
 
You spoke about your particular hardships...

175
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Erê wela, keko çê bikim dê zarokê tenê na.
 
Yes by God, brother, if I do it, I wouldn't leave the
children alone.

176
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Evana, nuh îro ji Efrînê hatine, ev meh zivistanê, ez û vîna
zarokê xwe em ê... dikişînin em rehet bibin.
 
These, newly came from Afrin today, this month is winter, me
and this one and my children will... weigh it so we can
rest.

177
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Tenê te ke jê nabe?
 
You can't do it alone?

178
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Nabe. Çê nabe.
 
No. It can't be done.

179
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Erê wellah yabo, em çêbikin.
 
Yes by God father, what can we do.

180
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Zeytûnê jî we gihîştinê. Welleh hûn bi me'nayî zêdetir acele
dikin şixulê xwe...
 
You also reached the olives. By God, we are suffering a lot,
we will harvest the olives...

181
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Wê maneyê hûn acele dikin şixulî xwe da.
 
Because of this reason you are hurrying in your work.

182
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Îsal baran jî, maşallah barî, zeytûn jî ketin erdê.
 
This year it also rained, mashallah it rained, the olives
also fell to the ground.

183
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Îsal di wextê xwe da zivistan hat. Wallahî yabo, îsal wextê
xwe da zivistan hat.
 
This year the winter came on time. By God father, this year
the winter came on time.

184
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Û maşallah zeytûn jî gişk hatin xwarê.
 
And mashallah all the olives came down.

185
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Darek heye, ew darê me ne.
 
There is a tree, those are our trees.

186
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Ew darên we li ser bîyê şikê ye?
 
Are your trees on the slope?

187
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Erê welle, a wî şikî ye...
 
Yes by God, they are on that slope...

188
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Bila bî ya Xwedê bî.
 
Let it be from God.

189
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:47,000
Nê ya qul bî. Em yê razî Xwedê ne...
 
Not from His servant. We are satisfied with God...

190
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Saet a te xweş. Xwedê emrêkî dirêj bide te. Taybet keça te
jî bextewer be Xwedê dîtina we.
 
Good job. May God give you a long life. Especially your
daughter should be happy, may God watch over you.

191
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Kêfxweş bî. Xwedê te ji Xwedê de te de tu jî qencîk bî yabo.
 
Be happy. May God give you from God so that you too will be
well, father.

192
00:13:55,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Em çêbikin yabo. Ev e jiyana me ye.
 
What can we do father. This is our life.

193
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Me em dîtin, ew kesên digel we rûniştî ne ya erebin, an em
di nav hev de çê nabin...
 
We saw, those people sitting with you are Arabs, or we can't
get along...

194
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Em dertk ji hev re nabin.
 
We don't have problems with each other.

195
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Na, dest ji hev ranabin... ew ne hatine qaçaẍa.
 
No, we don't let go of each other... they haven't come
smuggled.

196
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Em ji ne Ereb in mela. Hatine hîro em... Em nah du jiyên ji
maşallah ji mêj va em li ba hev dixebitin, em heval in.
 
We are not Arabs, mullah. They came today we... We, these
two women, mashallah, we have been working together for a
long time, we are friends.

197
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Herwiha ehîniya jî nîşanî dide...
 
Also it shows the dedication...

198
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Na duh jî, maşallah duh jî çi baran bû em av û heriyek bûn.
Me neçiniyê.
 
No yesterday too, mashallah yesterday what a rain it was, we
became water and mud. We didn't harvest.

199
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:24,000
Te çi gotin navê te Mistefo...
 
What did you say your name was, Mistefo...

200
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Tehşîn.
 
Tahseen.

201
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,000
Ez sipas dikim dayê.
 
I greet you mother.

202
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Ehlan welle babo. Em çêkin.
 
Welcome by God father. What can we do.

203
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Dibê qaçaxên Efrînê ta we haştina, va hesandin tiştek bû?
 
They say Afrin smugglers left it to you, did it make you
feel anything?

204
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Na na, wallah hefta ku ez û vî lawkî, em wisa xastin ha.
 
No no, by God it's a week that me and this boy, we wanted it
like this.

205
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Gelek we hesandine...
 
You have rested a lot...

206
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Na na, we hesandin nîne. Dar û mal şêrînin...
 
No no, there is no resting. Tree and house are sweet...

207
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Gava mirov rehet bûn, of of nakin.
 
When people are comfortable, they don't complain.

208
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:50,000
De Xwedê sihhet û qeweta bide de, û emrekî dirêj bide we jî
dayê.
 
May God give you health and strength, and a long life to you
too, mother.

209
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Em çê bikin babo. Heke baran nebûna zêdetir bû, lo... nîvê
şixul in.
 
What can we do father. If it hadn't rained it would have
been more... we are half working.

210
00:14:55,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Lê, ke pîşeyekî din doqire kî, bi destê... na meşe, elbet kê
pîşeng digre doqre... û tu jê ra natê û ti tişt nameşe.
 
But, someone shakes another branch by hand... it doesn't
work, of course someone holds the front and shakes... and
you don't keep up and nothing works.

211
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Ji wer re, ewana hin berhev dikin, keka Evdo jî hîna ew ku
çeng wan e, bîne ev verda ber da qetiya, paşê ew bar dikin
kîna jî...
 
For you, they are gathering some, brother Evdo is still
where their branch is, he brings it down until it breaks,
then they load those too...

212
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Erê, Xwedê rizqê we bide we.
 
Yes, may God give you your sustenance.

213
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Destpêkê, zêdetir ketine we, hinar bes e.
 
At the beginning, they have fallen more to you, pomegranate
is enough.

214
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Zêtûn jî, dêmis û ev tişt, pir acele dikin fena zeytûna wer
re...
 
Olives, syrup and these things, you are in a big hurry,
aren't you like that...

215
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Eh...
 
Yes...

216
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Eman ew kar girane wî ro.
 
But that work is heavy today.

217
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Em qir nakin.
 
We aren't harvesting.

218
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Wext zû derbas e.
 
Time passes quickly.

219
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Lê dema tu tê zeytûnê te dî, me malê gotî me divê em herin
zeytûnê kevin.
 
But when you came you saw the olives, we at the house said
we must go fall into the olives.

220
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Ew hinar jî ku sînê ket erdê, hinarî me giş gihîştin hev...
 
Those pomegranates also fell to the ground, all our
pomegranates ripened together...

221
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Pênc ferd em kar çêkin, em nakin zeytûnê berhev... Îca
tiştek waha nehiştin, em giş ber hev kin... Lê ev qet ji me
re dev nema... Xwedê bide...
 
Five individuals we are working, we don't gather olives...
So they didn't leave anything like this, we gather them
all... But this didn't leave a mouth for us... May God
give...

222
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,000
Ev nan çîçek û hejîrin?
 
Are these flowers and figs?

223
00:15:56,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Ew tenê em berhev dikin di hembêza torbe de em datînin avê.
 
Those we just gather in the embrace of the bag, we put them
in water.

224
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Em wan ê din jî wek wan li hev dixin û berhev dikin.
 
We also mix and gather the others like them.

225
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Me seh kir.
 
We heard.

226
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Aliya wan jî berhev kin... ev bavê... çawa ku rûyê din
derk... eweyî paş de qatirek der...
 
Gather their sides too... this father's... how the other
face comes out... the one in the back comes out like a
mule...

227
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Çawa xweş e em bi hev ra dikin... Wextê xwe nabînin... Wext
xweş derbas dibe.
 
How nice it is that we do it together... We don't see the
time... Time passes nicely.

228
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Ev cureyê hinarê çiye? Ev hinarê lefane?
 
What type of pomegranate is this? Is it lefan pomegranate?

229
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Na ev ne yê lefane.
 
No, these are not lefan.

230
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Ev ê me ferensî bûn. Çarsed dar in.
 
Ours were French. Four hundred trees.

231
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Me hilkirin. Hişk bûn, hişk bûn.
 
We uprooted them. They dried up, they dried up.

232
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Kurmê darê hate wan. Kurm ê hişk kirin.
 
The tree worm got to them. The worm dried them up.

233
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
Dayê destê te sax be, saeta we xweş be.
 
Mother, bless your hands, good job.

234
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Xwedê emrêkî dirêj bide we, destpêka we xweş bî, em bi
dîtina we kêfxweş bûn.
 
May God give you a long life, may your start be good, we
were happy to see you.

235
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Xwedê ji te razî be bavo.
 
May God be pleased with you father.

236
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Qusûra me nenêre jî, me we ji karê we kir..
 
Don't look at our faults, we kept you from your work..

237
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Na na de, bavo Xwedê Xwedê rizqê we jî binêre.
 
No no well, father may God provide your sustenance too.

238
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Xwedê te'bê we jî li boşa neke le.
 
May God not let your efforts go in vain.

239
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Silavê me ji gundî Kaniyê Gewrkê ra, ji bo tevahî ra heye.
 
We have greetings for the village of Kaniye Gewrke, for all
of them.

240
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Û ji malxwê te ra Xwedê emrêkî dirêj bide wî.
 
And for your husband, may God give him a long life.

241
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Xwedê ji te ra bide jî wilo.
 
May God give the same to you too.

242
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Te kesekî te heye ku tu silavê jê re bişîne jî?
 
Do you have anyone you would like to send greetings to?

243
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Xweşî be qizkê min heye.
 
Let it be good, I have my daughter.

244
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Silavên me ji qîza te ra heye. Xwedê rizqê wan bişîne...
 
