00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:16,000
Malê Beşîr digotin, Çoloqo hatine.
 
The Beşîr family, they said, the Çoloqo came.

379
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:22,000
Malê Hesen Mihemed digot, Cewer nizanim, Reşo ye, kî ye
hatine.
 
The Hesen Mihemed family used to say, Cewer I don't know,
it's Reşo, whoever it is has come.

380
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Mesela, malbata me mala Elîkê Neşê, kî ye, marî hatin.
 
For example, our family, the Elîkê Neşê family, whoever it
is, they came later.

381
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Yanî, hûn hemî ji, di her gundî de... apê Evdo, wek tu qala
dikî..
 
So, all of you, in every village... Uncle Evdo, as you
describe...

382
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:36,000
Her gundek, em dizanin ku malek û du mal ava kiriye an bi
hevre ev gund ava kirine...
 
Every village, we know that one house and two houses built
it, or together they built this village...

383
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:42,000
Eyyy. Ev cotarî bûn. Da û xebat. Yanî pênc-deh dihatin vî
gundî û dibûn gundî û dizivirin.
 
Yeah. They were farmers. They gave and worked. I mean, five-
ten would come to this village and become villagers and
return.

384
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Hinek xwedî gundên din, ji pîrekê dihatin, havînê vî gundî.
 
Some owning other villages, would come from a woman, to this
village in the summer.

385
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:55,000
Cot dikirin, dehl pûlê dikirin. Elmendê (Almendê) diçûn
gundê xwe, diçûn girtin... Yanî wisa. 50-60 sal em bi hevre
wisa derbas bûn.
 
They plowed, they did agriculture. Elmendê (Almendê), they
went to their village, they went to get it... So it goes.
50-60 years we spent together like this.

386
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:57,000
Û ew roj jî rojên we yên xweş bûn ku we wisa derbas bûn.
 
And those days were your good days that you spent like this.

387
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Xweş.
 
Good.

388
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Apê Evdo, gund Kaniyê Gewrikê wekê wextê xwe jî çend qism
bûn.
 
Uncle Evdo, the village of Kaniya Gewrikê was also divided
into a few sections in its time.

389
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:08,000
Mezlûm bûn gundiyan bi hev re. Milet bi hev re mezlûm bûn.
Wê çaxê... ne mezlûm bûn, yanî em wek mirovatiyê me gelek
hebû.
 
The villagers were oppressed together. The people were
oppressed together. At that time... they weren't oppressed,
I mean as humanity we had a lot.

390
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:11,000
Em dibînin ku berê gund Kaniyê Gewrikê du gund bûn.
 
We see that previously the village of Kaniya Gewrikê was two
villages.

391
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:22,000
Du tax bûn ev gund. Me ji taxê re digot Şêx Ebdurehman û
jêra... ev gundê din bû û yê jêrê... Ebdurehman.
 
This village was two neighborhoods. We used to call the
neighborhood Şêx Ebdurehman and the lower one... this was
the other village and the lower one... Ebdurehman.

392
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:24,000
Apê Evdo, di van herdu taxan de hûn bi çi dixebitîn?
 
Uncle Evdo, what did you work on in these two neighborhoods?

393
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:30,000
Ne, di van berya vê taxê de.. Ev li nava me gelek mal tune
bû. Ne xwedî bûn ev...
 
No, before this neighborhood in these... There weren't many
houses among us. They weren't owners...

394
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Apê Evdo, berê cotarî dihate xebatkirin li gund...
 
Uncle Evdo, formerly farming was worked in the village...

395
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Dikanên nû derketin?
 
Did new shops appear?

396
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Berê çawa bûn ev tişt?
 
How were these things before?

397
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Ne, me çi dikir? Tu dibînî bixwe, dihatin... Ne tu tiştên
giran tunebûn.
 
No, what did we do? You see for yourself, they came... There
were no heavy things.

398
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Îro ro, di demên zivistanê de gund Kaniyê Gewrikê tu hinekî
qal bikî. Wê çaxê, ew jiyana we hûn çi dixebitîn li gund?
Hûn piranî ji van karan...
 
Today, in the winter times, you talk a bit about the village
of Kaniya Gewrikê. Back then, your life, what did you work
on in the village? You mostly from these jobs...

399
00:27:54,000 --> 00:28:14,000
Li vî gundî me bêtir rez diçandin... zevî dikişandin û me
ceh, genimê xwe... Diçûn paletiyê dikirin. Em tev diçin
vî... Ev bêtir karê me yê rojane ev bû. Wek zeytûn me tunebû
li gund.
 
In this village we mostly planted vineyards... pulled fields
and our barley, wheat... They went to do harvesting. We all
go to this... This was mostly our daily work. Like we didn't
have olives in the village.

400
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:29,000
Hinar jî me wek dî nû hatin dîtin? Hinar we çawa dîtin li vê
herêmê? Hûn tenê, an bêtir? Kaniyê Gewrikê ma gundekî wiha
ye ku gundî av e... an ew mecala axê derket, an çawa derket
ev?
 
We also saw pomegranates recently? How did you find
pomegranates in this region? Only you, or more? Is Kaniya
Gewrikê such a village that the village is water... or did
the opportunity of the land arise, or how did this come
about?

401
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Em ê wiha bêjin mîrê min, me ji 50-60 salan vir ve... me
fêkiyên xwe ava kirine.
 
We will say it like this, my lord, since 50-60 years ago...
we established our fruits.

402
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

403
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:44,000
Ne wekî wan e ku hinek dibêjin em hinar çandine em hinar
difiroşin... Ne ku... Hîna tu xebat an yek tiştek hebû.
 
It's not like some who say we planted pomegranates, we sell
pomegranates... It wasn't... There was still no work or one
thing.

404
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Me dizanibû, te wî karî ji me re...
 
We knew, you did that job for us...

405
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Belê. Ez ê bi xwe çend gotinan bêjim da em fahm bikin... Li
ser vî wextî...
 
Yes. I myself will say a few words so we understand... On
this time...

406
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:59,000
Apê Evdo niha gund me ji te pirsî, gundekî çend malên kîjan
malbatan hebûn. We wiha di got.
 
Uncle Evdo, now we asked you about the village, a village of
how many houses from which families were there. You said so.

407
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:05,000
Min xwest bêjim di vê malbatê de hûn çi dikin? Ev kîjan wext
hatin vira bûn xwedî ax li van cihan?
 
I wanted to say what do you do in this family? When did
these come here and become landowners in these places?

408
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:10,000
Qedrê te, ez ê niha tiştekî bibêjim gundê derdorê em gundî
nas dikin.
 
With respect to you, I will say something now, we know the
villagers of the surrounding village.

409
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Niha em bi hinar dikin ev der... bi gelemperî hinar in.
Gundê wek min û yên din... Gundik mezin kiriye...
 
Now we are working with pomegranates here... generally it is
pomegranates. A village like mine and the others... The
hamlet has grown...

410
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:25,000
Apê Evdo em diçin ser kîjan alî gund, wî gundî me me dît,
gundiyên te bi rûyê geş digotin Apê Evdo.
 
Uncle Evdo, wherever we go in the village, we saw that
village, your villagers with bright faces used to say Uncle
Evdo.

411
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:34,000
Û dibêjin her kî we bibîne digot Evdo mirovekî merd e û
xwîngerm e, tu yê biçî li dîwanxaneya wî da rûnê qehwekî me
ji bîr nebe.
 
And they say whoever sees you said Evdo is a generous and
warm-blooded man, you will go sit in his guest house and
don't forget our coffee.

412
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Ev ne wek ku em mirovê baş in... ev karê min e ku ez ji vir
dibînim... hûn min digirin bi qedr...
 
This is not like we are good people... this is my job that I
see from here... you hold me in esteem...

413
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Hem qedr û hem jî mirov bi xwe re qenciyê dibîne, ev ji bo
gund, milet, nava gund da ew... ev şikl û rû bi we têkildar
e.
 
Both respect and one sees goodness with oneself, this is for
the village, the people, in the village it... this form and
face is related to you.

414
00:29:51,000 --> 00:30:11,000
Ê welle em jî hinek tiştên baş li gund dîtine... wek hûn...
em her tiştî li gor şiklên...
 
Well, we have also seen some good things in the village...
like you... we do everything according to the forms...

415
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Selamet, di xêrê da, Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
Blessings, in goodness, may God be pleased with you.

416
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:01,000
Dengê te sax be, destê te sax bin.
 
Bless your voice, bless your hands.

417
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:04,000
Lawo xwedê emrê te dirêj bike, te xêr hatî, te ser çava,
xwedê ji te razî be.
 
Boy, may God lengthen your life, welcome, upon my eyes, may
God be pleased with you.

418
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike, spas.
 
May God lengthen your life, thank you.

419
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:11,000
Xwedê bi yekê gotiye, ku her çar perçeyê Kurdistanê cem hev
bin, ev ketiye di vî dilî da, bîlahî xêra bavê te da ye.
 
God has truly said, that all four parts of Kurdistan should
be together, this has fallen into this heart, by God, it's
for the good of your father.

420
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:14,000
Anîko.
 
Exactly.

421
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:20,000
Dengê te sax be. Di vî dilê min de kelamek wisa heye dibêjim
qedrê we nîşan bidim, di nav da heye.
 
Bless your voice. There is such a word in this heart that I
want to show my respect to you, it's in here.

422
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:25,000
Dengê te sax be, Xwedê ji te razî be. Apê Ebdul, çend sal e
tu vê pîkê lê dixe?
 
Bless your voice, may God be pleased with you. Uncle Ebdul,
how many years have you been playing this flute?

423
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Lawo, ji mêj ve! Diwazdeh salê min çêbûn, min bal pismamê
xwe digirt. Gava derdiketim gundan û diçûmê, xwedê wisan
xistiye di min da.
 
Boy, for a long time! When I was twelve years old, I used to
stay with my cousin. Whenever I went out to the villages,
God put it in me like that.

424
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Bese ku ez didîtim ev mirovana ya, carna xêr, xêra xwe, min
pê xistiye navê.
 
Whenever I saw these people, sometimes for goodness, for
their sake, I started playing it.

425
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Gelek rind e, pîk rinde. Apê Ebdul, ji me re bi çîrokî de
çi...
 
It is very beautiful, the flute is beautiful. Uncle Ebdul,
tell us a story about what...

426
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:53,000
Erê min go Evdal e, Evdal e, Evdal e, lo Evdal e...
 
Yes, I said Evdal, Evdal, Evdal, oh Evdal...

427
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Erê bavo Hesen...
 
Yes, father Hesen...

428
00:31:54,000 --> 00:32:00,000
Min go Evdal e, bismam Evdal e, Evdal e, min qeda bira Evdal
e...
 
I said Evdal, cousin Evdal, Evdal, I take your troubles,
brother Evdal...

429
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:10,000
Lo belê lo Evdal e, Evdal e, emrê min telef kir Evdal lo...
 
Oh yes, oh Evdal, Evdal, you ruined my life, Evdal, oh...

430
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Min go lo bismam bilo lo gelo te roj hilat, Şerqî da, va
berê xwe dida çolê dinya xêr e...
 
I said, oh cousin, say it, oh, when the sun rose for you in
the East, you turned to the desert, the world is good...

431
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:24,000
Ne bi laşê Şemo Şeno kuro xwe bidî çar goşê dinê.
 
Do not give the body of Shemo Sheno, boy, to the four
corners of the world.

432
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:28,000
Bi ser de Çiyayê Mihemed, Sûka Bêrîstanê.
 
On top of that, Mount Mihemed, the Market of Beristan.

433
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:32,000
Kela Mêrdînê xwe nedî, siwarê ji Xana Sêwrekê.
 
You did not show yourself at the Castle of Mardin, the rider
from the Inn of Siverek.

434
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:40,000
Ciyê diyar be, kela Xûban da li pêsîrê...
 
Let the place be known, the Castle of Xuban is on the
slope...

435
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:45,000
Erê lo Evdal e, Evdal e, Evdal e, lo Evdal e...
 
Yes, oh Evdal, Evdal, Evdal, oh Evdal...

436
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:48,000
Bismam Evdal e, lo... Min qeda bira Evdal e...
 
Cousin Evdal, oh... I take your troubles, brother Evdal...

437
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:57,000
Belê bela Evdal e, lo... Emrê min telef kir Evdal lo...
 
Yes, trouble is Evdal, oh... You ruined my life, Evdal,
oh...

438
00:32:57,000 --> 00:33:08,000
Erê go lo bismam çima dibê? Ciyê bi bal e, neval e, xan û
deyan e, ciyê bilind e ser babê me da...
 
Yes, he said, oh cousin, why do you say that? The place is
high, it is a valley, inn and plains, the place is high
above our father...

439
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:14,000
Serê min qurbano, xebera pismamê te Hesenê Ehmed Begê...
 
I sacrifice my head, the news of your cousin Hesen son of
Ehmed Beg...

440
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Be pismamê te Hesen e, di meclîsê eşîran de, pey te re
bişîne...
 
Saying your cousin is Hesen, in the assembly of tribes, he
will send for you...

441
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Serê min qurbano, beza berdaye bi pêsîran, li dora xêman...
 
I sacrifice my head, they let running on the slopes, around
the tents...

442
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:31,000
Kela bi ecêban va ketiye li kenê lo...
 
The wondrous castle fell into laughter, oh...

443
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:37,000
Saet xweş, apê Ebdul. Saet xweş, Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike,
te xweş got. Dengê te sax be.
 
Good job, uncle Ebdul. Good job, may God lengthen your life,
you sang beautifully. Bless your voice.

444
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:41,000
Xwedê te ji me re bihêle. Ez gelekî kêfxweş im bi we, bi
rûniştina we, bi dîtina we.
 
May God keep you for us. I am very happy with you, with
sitting with you, with seeing you.

445
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:44,000
Xwedê te bihêle, ehlen wa sehlen...
 
May God protect you, welcome...

446
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:49,000
Şerefek mezin e ji me ra ku em cemaetek, her bavekî kurd ê
Efrînî wisa wekî te rûnin, hevdîtinek bikin.
 
It is a great honor for us to sit in a gathering with every
Kurdish elder from Afrin like you, and have a meeting.

447
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:50,000
Mî te ehlen we sehlen...
 
You are very welcome...

448
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Şerefek pir mezin e ji me re.
 
It is a very great honor for us.

449
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:57,000
Weke we gotiye xwaşmêran, hatina we, ev bo we... min ji
Xwedê dixwest...
 
As you brave men said, your coming, this for you... I was
asking God for this...

450
00:33:57,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Û em bi kêfxweşîyê, înşelah emê dîtinê jinûve bin, û emê hev
bibînin, saet xweş.
 
And we joyfully, hopefully will meet again, and we will see
each other, good job.

451
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Û silavê min ji milleta te re... ji her mirovekî eşîretê re.
 
And my greetings to your people... to every person of the
tribe.

452
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Û ji gundî... gundiyê Kanî Gewrikê giştan re û ji hosta
Cemîl, Mela Beşîr...
 
And to the village... all the villagers of Kani Gewrik and
to master Cemil, Mela Beshir...

453
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:12,000
Silavê min ji her însanek ku çandê hez dike, silavê min û ji
milletekî kurd teva heye.
 
My greetings go to every person who loves the culture, my
greetings go to the entire Kurdish nation.

454
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:17,000
Ez pir spasîya te dikim, ez zêde wextê te nagirim, kêm an
zêde eziyet bû, te emr da...
 
I thank you very much, I won't take too much of your time,
it was a bit of a hassle, you commanded...

455
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:21,000
Welle tiştek tunne, bi rastî, silametî ya we, saxbûna we.
 
By God it's nothing, really, it's your safety, your well-
being.

456
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:23,000
Xwedê ji te razî be, xwedê emrê te dirêj be.
 
May God be pleased with you, may God lengthen your life.

457
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:24,000
Xwedê emrê te jî.
 
May God lengthen your life too.

458
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:27,000
Xwedê te bihêle, apê Evdul.
 
May God protect you, uncle Evdul.

459
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:28,000
Û ummeta miletê teva.
 
And the entire nation.

460
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:48,000
Xwedê emrê te jî dirêj bike.
 
May God lengthen your life too.

461
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:05,000
Belê bînerên me yên ezîz, ez niha spasiya we dikim hûn me
bişopînin heta dawiya vîdyoyê.
 
Yes, our dear viewers, I now thank you for following us
until the end of the video.

462
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:08,000
Bîr nekin qenala me bi navê hevkariyê de aboneyê çêkin û
alîkariyê bidin.
 
Do not forget to subscribe to our channel in the name of
cooperation and support us.

463
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:10,000
Em spasîya vî gundî, tevahî dikin.
 
We thank this whole village.

464
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:12,000
Bi rastî istîqbalek pir xweş dan me, em pir kêfxweş bûn li
vî gundî.
 
Actually, they gave us a very nice welcome, we were very
happy in this village.

465
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:16,000
Ev carek din em derbasî gundê Kanî Gewrikê dibin. Yek gundê
xweş.
 
This is another time we are visiting the village of Kani
Gewrik. A beautiful village.

466
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Emê carek din da jî dîsa werin, emê gelek gundên din jî
biweşînin.
 
We will come back again, and we will broadcast many other
villages too.

467
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:21,000
Çi qusûr me hebe, lê biborînin. Silavên min ji her kesê ji
vî gundî re heye.
 
Forgive us if we have any shortcomings. My greetings go to
everyone from this village.

468
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:23,000
Û ji miletê kurd re teva heye.
 
And to the whole Kurdish nation.

469
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:39,000
Di bextê Xwedê de bin. Amade bin emê vîdyoyên xweştir ji we
re pêşkêş bikin.
 
May God protect you. Be ready, we will present more
beautiful videos to you.

470
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Lê lê, lê lê, lê lê, lê lê, lê lê, lê lê...
 
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh...

471
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Sebra dilê min lê lê, lê lê...
 
The patience of my heart, oh, oh...

472
00:35:56,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Mirat qebrê min lê lê, lê lê, lê lê...
 
The ruin of my grave, oh, oh, oh...

473
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:08,000
Sebebê serê min, lê lê... lê lê...
 
The cause of my ruin, oh, oh...

474
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Destdarê min lê lê... ay...
 
My supporter, oh... alas...

475
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:19,000
Anê bi pey de... dayê bi pey de...
 
Mother, let her go... mother, let her go...

476
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Anê bi pey de, lê lê dayê bi pey de...
 
Mother, let her go, oh mother, let her go...

477
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Bi lawikî şivan de, sozê min pê de...
 
Give her to the shepherd boy, give him my promise...

478
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:35,000
Bi lawikî şivan de, lê lê sozê min pê de...
 
Give her to the shepherd boy, oh, give him my promise...

479
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:40,000
Qelencê bibire, pênc sedî zêde...
 
Cut the bride price, add five hundred more...

480
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Bixwaze hezarî, lê lê, pênc sedî zêde...
 
Ask for a thousand, oh, add five hundred more...

481
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:55,000
Bi wan pênc sedî, de bila bide, xurê serê te sebebo, bi serê
xwe bide.
 
With those five hundred, let him pay it, may you bring
trouble upon your head, oh cause of ruin, bring it upon
yourself.

482
00:36:55,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Min anîye bi serê xwe bide, lê anê bi serê xwe bide.
 
I have brought it, bring it upon yourself, oh mother, bring
it upon yourself.

483
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Anê xizêmê, dayê xizêmê...
 
Mother with the nose ring, mother with the nose ring...

484
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:11,000
Anê xizêmê, lê lê, dayê xizêmê...
 
Mother with the nose ring, oh, mother with the nose ring...

485
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Anê xizêmê, lê lê, wena xizêmê...
 
Mother with the nose ring, oh, like a nose ring...

486
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:21,000
Lê lê wena xizêmê.
 
Oh, like a nose ring.

487
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:31,000
Eman eman dînê, dostê gulbarînê...
 
Oh, oh crazy one, friend of blooming roses...

488
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:37,000
Xulama dirkê te bim, yarê ser meşînê, dostê te nemînê.
 
Let me be the servant of your path, walking love, may your
friend not remain.

489
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:41,000
Yarê her meşîne...
 
Love is always walking...

490
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:48,000
Xulama dirkê te bim rî, yarê ser meşînê.
 
Let me be the servant of your path, walking love.

491
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:56,000
Dostê te nemînê, yarê her meşînê way...
 
May your friend not remain, walking love, alas...

492
00:37:56,000 --> 00:38:01,000
Helandim, şewitandim, kirim dar kevirînê.
 
You melted me, you burned me, you made me like a stone tree.

493
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:11,000
Eman eman dînê, dostê gulbarînê, yarê xeyidînê.
 
Oh, oh crazy one, friend of blooming roses, the offended
love.

494
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:23,000
Eman eman dînê, dostê gulbarînê, yarê xew revînê...
 
Oh, oh crazy one, friend of blooming roses, the sleep-
stealing love...

495
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:27,000
Binê mala me avdar e, piştî mala me avdar e.
 
Below our house is watery, behind our house is watery.

496
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:40,000
Binê mala me avdar e, piştî mala me avdar e, bexçeyek l'
hinar e, bexçeyek l' hinar e...
 
Below our house is watery, behind our house is watery, there
is a pomegranate garden, there is a pomegranate garden...

497
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:47,000
Tirba bavê we Urfê ye, tirba bavê we Urfê ye, mêratê
xwînwêran e, wey yarê...
 
The tomb of your father is in Urfa, the tomb of your father
is in Urfa, the cursed blood ruins, oh love...

498
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:53,000
Mêratê xwînwêran e.
 
The cursed blood ruins.

499
00:38:53,000 --> 00:38:58,000
Lê Urfê, lê Urfê, lê Urfê şêrîn Urfê...
 
Oh Urfa, oh Urfa, oh sweet Urfa...

500
00:38:58,000 --> 00:39:12,000
Lê Urfê delal Urfê... lê Urfê şêrîn Urfê... lê Urfê delal
Urfê... lê Urfê te bi nav Urfê... lê Urfê...
 
Oh beautiful Urfa... oh sweet Urfa... oh beautiful Urfa...
oh renowned Urfa... oh Urfa...

501
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:22,000
Çol ser xaniyê me dimeşe... lê lê hat la min... xaniyê kule
ax diweşe lê lê rindam min.
 
The desert walks over our house... oh she came to me... the
house of sorrow sheds soil, oh my beautiful one.

502
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:32,000
Çol ser xaniyê me dimeşe, lê lê hat la min. Xaniyê ku le ax
diweşe, lê lê rindam min.
 
The desert walks over our house, oh she came to me. The
house of sorrow sheds soil, oh my beautiful one.

503
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:37,000
Qevd şikiyê da kef xwaş e... lê lê hat la min...
 
She is joyful in the broken bundle... oh she came to me...

